{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: forecasts are systematically too high vs. realized prices, especially beyond ~day 8–10. Apply a downward level shift (increasing with horizon).",
    "Downtrend underestimation / lag: when the recent history is falling, the model projects stabilization/rebound too early; realized path keeps declining. Add extra negative drift proportional to recent 10–20d slope.",
    "Overshoot on rebounds: the model repeatedly predicts sharp recoveries to low/mid-70s that do not materialize (true stays mid-60s). Damp mean-reversion strength; cap rebound magnitude after sell-offs.",
    "Horizon-dependent error growth: near-term (days 1–5) errors are small; medium/long horizon errors widen materially. Use a horizon-weighted correction (minimal for days 1–5, moderate for 6–10, strong for 11–30).",
    "Volatility overprojection: forecast paths are too wavy (higher amplitude) than outcomes. Apply smoothing/shrinkage of day-to-day changes toward a monotone continuation of the prevailing trend."
  ]
}
